			SUBSEC 3.3.7.
				Disclosures in case of considerable delay in providing information by the
	SUBPART - Issuer:
				PARA a.
					As  per  Regulation  18(2)  of  SEBI  (CRA)  Regulations,  1999,  the  CRA,  while covering  the  analysis  of  the  various  factors  justifying  the  assessment  in  press release, shall also disclose the factors constituting a risk.
				PARA b.
					Accordingly,  it  is  further  clarified  that  if  the  issuer  does  not  share  information sought  by  the  CRA  within  7  days  of  seeking  such  information  from  the  Issuer, even  after  repeated  reminders  (within  these  7  days)  from  the  CRA,  the  CRA shall  take  appropriate  rating  action  depending  upon  the  severity  of  information risk of the issuer.
				{{IMG media/Image231.png}}
				PARA c.
					The Press Release in such cases shall mention the efforts made by the CRA in seeking such information and limitations regarding such information availability.
			SUBSEC 3.3.8.
				Disclosures in case of rating not accepted by an issuer
				PARA a.
					Each CRA shall disclose on its  website details  of all ratings assigned by them, irrespective of whether the rating is accepted by the issuer or not, even in case of  non-public  issues.  Details  disclosed  shall  include  the  name  of  the  issuer, name/ type of instrument, size of the issue, rating and outlook assigned, etc.
			SUBSEC 3.3.9.
				Disclosures in case of delay in periodic review
				PARA a.
					Each CRA shall promptly disclose on its website details of all such ratings where the  review  became  due  but  was  not  completed  by  the  due  date,  as  per  the timelines  specified  in  the  CRA's  Operations  Manual/  Internal  governing document. Details disclosed shall include the name of the issuer, name/ type of instrument,  size  of  the  issue,  date  of  last  review,  reasons  for  delay  in  periodic review, hyperlink to the last Press Release, etc.
			SUBSEC 3.3.10.
				Disclosure of guidelines for dealing with Conflict of Interest:{{^{{FOOTNOTE 29}}}}
				FOOTNOTE 29
					SEBI Circular No. CIR/MIRSD/6/2013 dated August 28, 2013
				PARA a.
					The policies adopted by the CRAs for effective implementation of guidelines for dealing  with  Conflict  of  Interest  for  investment/  trading  by  CRAs,  Access Persons and other employees, shall be disclosed on the CRAs' website.
				{{IMG media/Image235.png}}
